# The first filters: the filters that a list of binary naturals and its
# elements get from the constants up, with no occurrence tag. A class is typed when it holds the choice x + (x ∥ T), the
# convention of hindley_milner_unions' candidates; each lemma writes that
# choice into the class of its left side, and each left side matches its
# arguments' classes in that form. T is read from the head's filter in the
# term, never chosen, and the nine lemmas are the same whatever a list's length.
#
# Zero is the one constant whose filtered member is closed: binary_zero ∥
# binary_set true is wren_typed_zero of wren_typed_block, a noinline leaf of
# the e-graph wherever that file's leaves are read, and e-matching never looks
# into a leaf. So zero's class holds binary_zero + wren_typed_zero, which the
# pattern x + (x ∥ T) does not match, and three lemmas read that form where a
# zero head or argument meets one: wren_first_filter_odd_of_zero, and
# wren_first_filter_singleton_of_zero and wren_first_filter_cons_of_zero.
# Measured on the IR 2026-11-21 (repeated_library_edit_distances_small, direct,
# one repetition, seed 20261116, the knowledge of contest-entries-wren): the six
# lemmas without these three added 4 instances and no parallel; without
# wren_typed_block's knowledge they typed 240 of the 241 cons cells by
# list_type (binary_set true).
#
# Every lemma is (6), M + (M ∥ N) = M, read right to left with M its left
# side, except wren_first_filter_widening, whose two sides each equal x by
# (6) (CONTRIBUTING.md, "Terms"); so each holds up to ≃_O whatever its
# filter (the paper proof absorption).
# Whether a filter is true decides only whether a typed path is taken. On
# canonical binary constants every filter these lemmas write is true: zero is
# a canonical natural (binary_set true); 2h + 1 is a canonical positive
# natural (binary_set false) for every canonical h, and 2h is one for every
# canonical positive h, while binary_even binary_zero is matched by no lemma;
# a canonical positive natural is a canonical natural; and a cons of a member
# of T onto nil or onto a member of list_type T is a member of list_type T.
#
# Termination, derived and not proved, in a round with no built-in rule:
# wren_first_filter_zero has no metavariable and matches once; widening adds
# binary_set true and writes no binary_set false, so it does not feed itself;
# a class holds at most the two element filters, so each application of
# binary_odd or binary_even in the input is matched at most once by its
# lemma, and each cons cell at most twice, once for each filter of its head;
# no right side adds an application of binary_odd, binary_even or cons, and
# the applications of list_type it adds are matched by no left side.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero binary_even binary_odd _ binary_set
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "native_types") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "native_types") "list")
λ nil cons _ list_type
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "wren_typed_block") "wren_typed_block")
λ _ _ wren_typed_zero _ _ _ _ _ _
. export
λ _ rewriting _ _
. rewriting
λ _ lemmas _
. lemmas
  # A cons of a head typed by T onto a tail typed by list_type T is typed by
  # list_type T.
  ( λ s
    . s
      (λk. k "wren_first_filter_cons")
      (λx_0 x_1 x_2. cons (x_0 ∥ x_1 + x_0) (x_2 ∥ list_type x_1 + x_2))
      ( λ x_0 x_1 x_2
        . ( cons (x_0 ∥ x_1 + x_0) (x_2 ∥ list_type x_1 + x_2)
          ∥ list_type x_1
          + cons (x_0 ∥ x_1 + x_0) (x_2 ∥ list_type x_1 + x_2)
          )
      ) λ_ md _. md λk. k "[absorption](docs/design/gezi-hindley-milner-unions-proofs.md#absorption)"
  # A cons of a head typed by T onto nil is typed by list_type T.
  + λ s
    . s
      (λk. k "wren_first_filter_singleton")
      (λx_0 x_1. cons (x_0 ∥ x_1 + x_0) nil)
      (λx_0 x_1. (cons (x_0 ∥ x_1 + x_0) nil ∥ list_type x_1 + cons (x_0 ∥ x_1 + x_0) nil))
      λ_ md _. md λk. k "[absorption](docs/design/gezi-hindley-milner-unions-proofs.md#absorption)"
  # A value typed by the canonical positive naturals is typed by the canonical
  # naturals: both sides are x by (6).
  + λ s
    . s
      (λk. k "wren_first_filter_widening")
      (λx_0. (x_0 ∥ binary_set false + x_0))
      (λx_0. (x_0 ∥ binary_set true + x_0))
      λ_ md _. md λk. k "[absorption](docs/design/gezi-hindley-milner-unions-proofs.md#absorption)"
  # 2h of a canonical positive h is a canonical positive natural.
  + λ s
    . s
      (λk. k "wren_first_filter_even")
      (λx_0. binary_even (x_0 ∥ binary_set false + x_0))
      ( λ x_0
        . ( binary_even (x_0 ∥ binary_set false + x_0)
          ∥ binary_set false
          + binary_even (x_0 ∥ binary_set false + x_0)
          )
      ) λ_ md _. md λk. k "[absorption](docs/design/gezi-hindley-milner-unions-proofs.md#absorption)"
  # 2h + 1 of a canonical h is a canonical positive natural.
  + λ s
    . s
      (λk. k "wren_first_filter_odd")
      (λx_0. binary_odd (x_0 ∥ binary_set true + x_0))
      ( λ x_0
        . ( binary_odd (x_0 ∥ binary_set true + x_0)
          ∥ binary_set false
          + binary_odd (x_0 ∥ binary_set true + x_0)
          )
      ) λ_ md _. md λk. k "[absorption](docs/design/gezi-hindley-milner-unions-proofs.md#absorption)"
  # Zero is a canonical natural.
  + λ s
    . s (λk. k "wren_first_filter_zero") binary_zero (binary_zero ∥ binary_set true + binary_zero)
      λ_ md _. md λk. k "[absorption](docs/design/gezi-hindley-milner-unions-proofs.md#absorption)"
  # 2h + 1 of zero typed by its typed version is a canonical positive natural.
  + λ s
    . s
      (λk. k "wren_first_filter_odd_of_zero")
      (λx_0. binary_odd (wren_typed_zero + x_0))
      (λx_0. (binary_odd (wren_typed_zero + x_0) ∥ binary_set false + binary_odd (wren_typed_zero + x_0)))
      λ_ md _. md λk. k "[absorption](docs/design/gezi-hindley-milner-unions-proofs.md#absorption)"
  # A cons of zero typed by its typed version onto nil is typed by list_type
  # (binary_set true).
  + λ s
    . s
      (λk. k "wren_first_filter_singleton_of_zero")
      (λx_0. cons (wren_typed_zero + x_0) nil)
      ( λ x_0
        . ( cons (wren_typed_zero + x_0) nil
          ∥ list_type (binary_set true)
          + cons (wren_typed_zero + x_0) nil
          )
      ) λ_ md _. md λk. k "[absorption](docs/design/gezi-hindley-milner-unions-proofs.md#absorption)"
  # A cons of zero typed by its typed version onto a tail typed by list_type
  # (binary_set true) is typed by list_type (binary_set true).
  + λ s
    . s
      (λk. k "wren_first_filter_cons_of_zero")
      (λx_0 x_1. cons (wren_typed_zero + x_0) (x_1 ∥ list_type (binary_set true) + x_1))
      ( λ x_0 x_1
        . ( cons (wren_typed_zero + x_0) (x_1 ∥ list_type (binary_set true) + x_1)
          ∥ list_type (binary_set true)
          + cons (wren_typed_zero + x_0) (x_1 ∥ list_type (binary_set true) + x_1)
          )
      ) λ_ md _. md λk. k "[absorption](docs/design/gezi-hindley-milner-unions-proofs.md#absorption)"
  )
